  <!-- Why Linxira -->
  <section class="section-block section-block-alt">
    <div class="section">
      <div class="section-header">
        <h2 class="section-title">Why Linxira</h2>
        <p class="section-subtitle">One distribution that does both: daily desktop and scientific computing</p>
        <div class="section-divider"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="features">
        <div class="feature"><span class="feature-icon">🖥️</span><h3>Direct Arch Desktop</h3><p>KDE Plasma built directly on the Arch official repositories — always current, always fast. Dual kernels (linux + linux-lts) as the rolling-update safety net.</p></div>
        <div class="feature"><span class="feature-icon">📦</span><h3>93 Curated Apps</h3><p>An audited software catalog: containers, dev tools, scientific apps, AI tooling… check boxes in the installer, no hunting through repositories.</p></div>
        <div class="feature"><span class="feature-icon">🔐</span><h3>Signed [linxira] Repo</h3><p>All 17 first-party tools ship through our own signing key, tracked by pacman — from Welcome to Config Hub, one chain of trust.</p></div>
        <div class="feature"><span class="feature-icon">🛡️</span><h3>Rolling-Update Safety</h3><p>Timeshift automatic snapshots + grub-btrfs boot-time rollback + dual-kernel fallback. A broken update costs a reboot, not a reinstall.</p></div>
        <div class="feature"><span class="feature-icon">🐳</span><h3>Container Reproducibility</h3><p>Podman, Distrobox and Apptainer out of the box — pull others' environments, reproduce results, publish your own images. Near-zero overhead.</p></div>
        <div class="feature"><span class="feature-icon">⚡</span><h3>Headless Mode</h3><p>One command drops to a command-line target: zero desktop memory, all RAM for compute. Back to the desktop any time. Your PC is a mini supercomputer.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Who it's for -->
  <section class="section-block">
    <div class="section">
      <div class="about-grid">
        <div class="about-text">
          <h3>Who it's for</h3>
          <p>Linxira is built for <strong>science students, researchers and developers</strong>: people who need an everyday computer that can also become a compute machine.</p>
          <p>Most distributions favor either desktop comfort or server capability — rarely both. Linxira keeps the <strong>full desktop</strong> (Bluetooth, Wi-Fi, printing, graphical environment all work out of the box) and adds what research actually needs: <strong>memory tuning, headless mode, container reproducibility</strong>. Not a "mini server" — a desktop supercomputer.</p>
          <p>And critically, <strong>installation needs no network</strong>: the ISO bundles a complete offline package source, so a full usable system installs even on campus or intranet networks.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="about-stats">
          <div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-num">93</div><div class="stat-label">Curated apps</div></div>
          <div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-num">17</div><div class="stat-label">First-party tools</div></div>
          <div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-num">804</div><div class="stat-label">Offline packages</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

